# Credential shape for bases-mcp.
//
// Names, types and examples; never a value. There is no `.env.example` to keep
// in step with — this file is the single source of truth.
//
// The vault is chosen by the environment: `BASES_MCP_VAULT` names a vault
// mounted into the container, `BASES_MCP_WEBDAV_*` a remote one. Exactly one
// backend is used, and `BASES_MCP_VAULT` wins if both are set. These are the
// variables an operator must plant; the renderer requests them as podman secrets
// and they arrive at /run/secrets/<KEY>.

// @defaultSensitive=true

// BASES_MCP_VAULT
//   @sensitive
//   @example /vault

// BASES_MCP_WEBDAV_URL
//   @sensitive

// BASES_MCP_WEBDAV_USER
//   @sensitive

// BASES_MCP_WEBDAV_PASSWORD
//   @sensitive
